  {"k": "⚽ The Cup Final", "lines": ["On a wet Saturday in April, Darragh's under-14 team travelled to Thurles for the cup final.", "At half-time they were losing by three goals, and their captain was injured.", "At that moment, Darragh, the smallest player on the team, was sent on.", "Slowly, the team fought back, point by point.", "Finally, the whistle blew, and the cup was theirs by a single point."]},
  {"k": "🐴 The Pony", "lines": ["Every summer, Niamh stayed on her uncle's farm near Ennis.", "Then she found the gate open and her pony, Biscuit, gone.", "Just then, she heard hooves on the road and saw Biscuit trotting home beside a farmer.", "Afterwards, Niamh and her uncle fixed the latch on the gate.", "From that day on, she checked the gate twice before bed."]},
  {"k": "🎻 The Concert", "lines": ["It was a cold December evening, and Oisín was about to play the fiddle at the school concert.", "Halfway through his tune, a string broke, and someone in the front row laughed.", "Without warning, his granny started clapping the beat from the back of the hall.", "Bit by bit, the whole hall joined in, and Oisín kept playing on three strings.", "At last, he took a bow to the loudest cheer of the concert."]},
  {"k": "🌊 The Island", "lines": ["On a calm July morning, Cara and her dad rowed out to a tiny island off Connemara.", "While they explored, the rope came loose, and their boat was gone.", "Suddenly, Cara spotted the boat caught on a rock at the far end of the island.", "Afterwards, they waded out, soaked to the knees, and pulled it free.", "In the end, they rowed home laughing, with a story to tell everyone."]},
  {"k": "🐶 The Neighbour", "lines": ["Every afternoon after school, Tadhg walked past old Mr Flynn's house in Mallow.", "Mr Flynn shouted at him for kicking a ball against his wall, and Tadhg refused to say sorry.", "Just then, Mr Flynn's dog slipped its lead and ran towards the busy road.", "After that, Tadhg carried the dog back, and Mr Flynn shook his hand.", "From that day on, Tadhg walked the dog for him every weekend."]},
  {"k": "📖 The Diary", "lines": ["It was the first week of the summer holidays, and Aoife was clearing out Gran's attic in Sligo.", "She found an old diary, but the last pages were torn out.", "At that moment, a folded letter slipped out of the cover.", "Slowly, she read Gran's story of leaving home at fifteen.", "In the end, Aoife and Gran read the diary together over a pot of tea."]},
  {"k": "⛰️ The Hike", "lines": ["On a misty October morning, Liam's scout group set off up Galtymore.", "Near the top, the fog grew thicker and Liam realised they were lost.", "All at once, the fog lifted and they saw the path below them.", "Slowly, the group picked its way back down the mountain.", "By the end of the hike, Liam was the one leading the way."]},
  {"k": "🎭 The School Play", "lines": ["In the spring term, Shauna's class was putting on a play in the parish hall.", "Two days before the show, the lead actor missed rehearsal and rain ruined the scenery.", "Suddenly, the teacher handed the script to Shauna, who knew every line.", "After that, the class painted new scenery every lunchtime.", "Finally, the curtain came down and the whole hall rose to its feet."]},
  {"k": "🐦 The Robin", "lines": ["On a frosty January morning, Kevin found a robin on his doorstep in Tralee.", "Its wing was broken and it couldn't fly.", "Just then, his sister came home with a shoebox and a warm towel.", "Afterwards, Kevin fed the robin every day for three weeks.", "At last, he opened the box, and the robin flew to the top of the hedge."]},
  {"k": "🎨 The Mural", "lines": ["On the first Monday of the Easter holidays, Fionn started painting a mural on the youth-club wall.", "Overnight, someone sprayed paint across it, and the mural was ruined.", "Without warning, the boy who had sprayed it walked up and picked up a brush.", "Bit by bit, the two of them painted over the damage together.", "In the end, the mural had both their names in the corner."]},
  {"k": "🧳 The Move", "lines": ["It was a hot August afternoon when Ellen's family moved from Dublin to a farm in Leitrim.", "She missed her friends, and the local girls ignored her at the bus stop.", "Suddenly, a calf got out onto the road, and only Ellen knew how to calm it.", "After that, the girls asked her to show them how she did it.", "From that day on, Leitrim felt like home."]}
